    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1278">

                <pb facs="1018" n="902" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg902"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 612.1123/5.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the American Chargé
                        d’Affaires</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-10-26T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 26, 1912—4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s telegram October 23, 1 p.m., your October 24, 12 noon. The
                    Department desires you to communicate to the Mexican Government the position of
                    the United States regarding the closure <pb facs="1019" n="903" xml:id="pg903"/>
                    of the ports as instructed in the Department’s said telegram, explaining that
                    the telegram was sent prior to the receipt of news of the recapture of Vera
                    Cruz.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
